+- [Should-fix] §2.2a "no C0/C1 control characters other than `\t`, `\n` and `\r` (so no ESC)" — A bare carriage return is admitted anywhere in instruction content. Printed raw in the plan diff (§2.4 `plan::commands::render`, §3.3 tty prompt), `\r` returns the cursor to column 0 so later text overwrites earlier text; `do X\rdo Y` shows as `do Y` while the model receives both. The iteration-1 fix shape allowed only `\n` and `\t`. (regressed from iteration 1 "§2.2 UTF-8-only validation": fix incomplete) [lanes: regression] [fix-regression]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Spec line 57 admits `\r` with no CRLF restriction; the invisible-code-point list that follows does not mention CR. §2.4 lines 64-67 print each effect's diff as an indented block with no escaping; LineDiff is specified as a raw LCS unified diff. Grep for render, escape, terminal, CRLF, invisible finds no other rule handling `\r`. §3.5 residuals do not include display spoofing through the diff.
+  fix-shape hint: Admit `\r` only when immediately followed by `\n` (keeps CRLF files working), or reject it and have the diff renderer escape control characters visibly.
